<title>TUNISIA: Tunisian auction raises 54.4 million dinars.</title>
<headline>Tunisian auction raises 54.4 million dinars.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tunisian Treasury raised 54.4 million dinars at its weekly auction of treasury bills dated April 15, and repaid maturing paper totalling 12.6 million dinars.</p>
<p>Rate for two-year notes payable at maturity was down to 6.8750 percent coupon rate from 6.9375 percent last week, but two-year notes payable in equal annual tranches were priced up at 6.8750 percent coupon rate from 6.8125 percent previously.</p>
<p>Herewith breakdown of the auction results:</p>
<p> Maturity		    Amount   Rate   Previous week</p>
<p>-Two-year note payable in</p>
<p> equal annual tranches    20 MD   6.8750     6.8125</p>
<p>				  20 MD   6.9375     6.0750</p>
<p>				  12.4MD  7.0000     6.9375</p>
<p>				  -	   -	  7.0000</p>
<p>-Two-year note payable</p>
<p> at maturity		  0.5 MD  6.8750     6.9375</p>
<p>				  1.5 MD  6.9375     7.0000</p>
<p>				  50.0 MD 7.1250	 -</p>
<p>Banks bid for 261 million dinars for two-year and three-year notes at between 6.8750 and 7.5 percent. (one $=1.09 dinar)</p>
<p>--Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538  REUTER AB</p>
